From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weiyi Feng <fwy1998@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:25:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hosted: return an empty property dictionary for nubs with no
 property table

dictionaryWithProperties() called getPropertyTable()->getCapacity() and
OSDictionary::withDictionary() unguarded. Some hosted nubs never get a
property table, so io_service_get_matching_service (which walks every
service for _copyPropertiesForMatching) faulted, in ramrod. Return an
empty dictionary instead. With this and the world-switch UMIP clear, the
recovery launchd runs the whole boot sequence and reboots deliberately.
---
 iokit/Kernel/IORegistryEntry.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IORegistryEntry.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IORegistryEntry.cpp
index ef6b6ed..5685e43 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IORegistryEntry.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IORegistryEntry.cpp
@@ -573,6 +573,12 @@ IORegistryEntry::dictionaryWithProperties( void ) const
 {
 	OSDictionary *      dict;
 
+	/* BERINGIA: some hosted nubs never get a property table; matching must see an empty dictionary, not a
+	 * NULL dereference (io_service_get_matching_service walks every service). */
+	if (!getPropertyTable()) {
+		return OSDictionary::withCapacity(1);
+	}
+
 	PLOCK;
 	dict = OSDictionary::withDictionary( getPropertyTable(),
 	    getPropertyTable()->getCapacity());
